 "text": "Hey! How's your day been so far? Totally normal worry. People do look at their plates while you' eating, and they usually assume you' sharing. If you catch someone eyeing you, a quick wave helps. If it' really windy, the waiter will set a table cloth over the forks as they leave. You can always ask them to do that. Most places these days don't really care, as long as you' reasonably clean and not too flashy. If you' worried, wear something classic. Then ask the waiter to explain anything you' unsure about. Most people do that and it makes you look smart, not stupid. Definitely. It's short way of seeing what the place is like without commitment. Lots of places these days even let you taste two or three dishes from the main menu.",
